                            <comment id="495066" author="JIRAUSER19288" created="Wed, 27 May 2026 10:16:10 +0000">&lt;p&gt;+1 sanityn test_71c: &lt;a href="https://testing.whamcloud.com/test_sets/336d79c3-ac4d-45cc-a9cb-d89cd5ddefd6" class="external-link" target="_blank" rel="nofollow noopener"&gt;https://testing.whamcloud.com/test_sets/336d79c3-ac4d-45cc-a9cb-d89cd5ddefd6&lt;/a&gt; &lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="496631" author="adilger" created="Tue, 23 Jun 2026 07:34:05 +0000">&lt;p&gt;This crashed about 90x in the past four weeks, exclusively on ZFS.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;It looks like the crash is in ofd_destroy() for the cases I checked, which is a bit surprising since I wouldn't expect destroy to be using a lot of memory. Lustre itself is only using 148MiB of 3GiB on the VM, but that does not include page cache or ARC. &lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="496716" author="emoly.liu" created="Wed, 24 Jun 2026 06:59:37 +0000">&lt;p&gt;+1 on master: &lt;a href="https://testing.whamcloud.com/test_sets/f925fa5b-c83f-41ca-9c5d-eb4c157819ba" class="external-link" target="_blank" rel="nofollow noopener"&gt;https://testing.whamcloud.com/test_sets/f925fa5b-c83f-41ca-9c5d-eb4c157819ba&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="497931" author="adilger" created="Mon, 13 Jul 2026 23:36:56 +0000">&lt;p&gt;+13 OOM crashes in test_70b the past week:&lt;br/&gt;
&lt;a href="https://testing.whamcloud.com/search?status%5B%5D=CRASH&amp;amp;test_set_script_id=570ba67a-4a46-11e0-a7f6-52540025f9af&amp;amp;sub_test_script_id=52c5a802-7bc4-11e2-8242-52540035b04c&amp;amp;start_date=2026-07-07&amp;amp;end_date=2026-07-13&amp;amp;source=sub_tests#redirect" class="external-link" target="_blank" rel="nofollow noopener"&gt;https://testing.whamcloud.com/search?status%5B%5D=CRASH&amp;amp;test_set_script_id=570ba67a-4a46-11e0-a7f6-52540025f9af&amp;amp;sub_test_script_id=52c5a802-7bc4-11e2-8242-52540035b04c&amp;amp;start_date=2026-07-07&amp;amp;end_date=2026-07-13&amp;amp;source=sub_tests#redirect&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;It is always failing on the OSS node.  The sanityn test_70b test itself does not create or delete many files, so it is confusing why it is hitting OOM.  I suspect some kind of strange overflow/underflow in the size calculation, or possibly some bad interaction between osd-zfs and the new ZFS 2.4.0 code that is being run for the past few months.&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
